From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 03:35:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: dispatch TCP ACK flows to high-priority queues

Bulk data queueing behind ACKs starves the return path on asymmetric
links. Partition the TX queue space into data (lower half) and ACK
(upper half) at offset num_tx_queues / 2 on netsys v2+ and offset 6 on
v1 (where the 4-bit MTK_FOE_IB2_QID caps qid at 15). Classify
ACK-dominant flows via conntrack accounting (mean packet size <= 64 B
and fewer packets than peer) and bump the qid by
mtk_pppq_ack_queue_offset(eth). Thread struct flow_offload through
flow_cls_offload so the offloader can reach the conntrack entry.

Based-on-patch-by: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Kubik <piotr.kubik@adtran.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
